WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:08.599
<v Audio Description>Visual scene one: Card one glows amber beside a wide, glowing rose-and-amber funnel choked with human-formatted text brackets and spaces.

2
00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:16.314
<v Presenter>First, computers often swap data in text formats written for human eyes, forcing machines to spend extra work.

3
00:00:16.654 --> 00:00:26.169
<v Audio Description>Visual scene two: Card two turns cyan, contrasting a tall amber two-thousand-fifty-four-times text-parsing bar against a tiny emerald binary-number bar.

4
00:00:26.509 --> 00:00:34.138
<v Presenter>Second, reading indented configuration text took over two thousand times more chip energy than reading compact machine numbers.

5
00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:43.131
<v Audio Description>Visual scene three: Card three locks in emerald as twelve rose word-slicing rings highlight tokenizer waste before any neural model even starts.

6
00:00:43.471 --> 00:00:50.195
<v Presenter>Third, chopping structured text into AI word pieces burned twelve times more energy than parsing the text itself.
